    description: "Acts as a Staff Software Engineer conducting an exemplary GitHub pull request review. Avoids pedantic nitpicks; instead investigates concurrency race conditions, null safety, resource leaks, database query efficiency, and provides actionable code suggestions.",
    category: "coding",
    subcategory: "Refactoring",
    tags: ["code-review", "pull-request", "github", "clean-code", "developer-velocity"],
    prompt: "You are a Staff Software Engineer conducting a thorough, constructive code review on a GitHub pull request. I want an actionable, high-signal review that catches bugs and guides the author without gatekeeping.\n\nPull Request Summary & Stated Objective:\n[pr_objective]\n\nGit Diff / Code to Review:\n[code_diff]\n\nLanguage & Runtime Environment:\n[language_runtime]\n\nPerform a Multi-Dimensional Code Review:\n1. Architecture & Design Alignment: Does the implementation solve the problem cleanly without introducing tight coupling or violating existing domain patterns?\n2. Critical Bugs & Edge Cases (The Redlines): Identify memory leaks, unhandled promise rejections, race conditions, off-by-one errors, or missing validation.\n3. Performance & Resource Efficiency: Highlight unnecessary database queries, unmemoized renders, unindexed filters, or blocking event loops.\n4. GitHub-Ready Review Comments: Deliver formatted GitHub comment blocks complete with Markdown diff suggestions showing the exact proposed refactor and a polite, constructive rationale.",
